@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Edit planned fields and story scope
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "SprintPlanningPage / SprintPlanView\nor SprintFormDialog / SprintForm" as page
  participant "ISprintService / SprintService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "SprintsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "SaveSprintPlanCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "Sprint" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
actor -> page : Save plan fields (SprintForm) or the pending story changes (SprintPlanView)
page -> client : SaveSprintPlanCommand: workspace, sprint, expected version, fields, addStoryIds, removeStoryIds\n(SprintForm sends both sets empty; pending sets come from every page and search, including an add or remove pre-mark)
client -> access : PUT /api/workspaces/{id}/sprints/{sprintId}/plan
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once; sign in with the planning page as return route
else Authenticated (profile P: every active role plans sprints)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send SaveSprintPlanCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : L2-022 trim; field limits, valid dates, end on or after start;\ndistinct IDs; no story in both sets
  alt Missing, over-limit or malformed fields; end before start; duplicate or contradictory IDs
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; nothing read or changed
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : Keep all input and pending sets; one field error focuses that field, which reads\nits error; several focus the linked error summary; no Retry or reference ID
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle SaveSprintPlanCommand
    handler -> db : BeginWorkspaceTransactionAsync (workspace lock); LoadPlanChangeAsync:\nmode, Sprint with status and version and the memberships to remove as tracked children,\nstories to add with their open memberships
    db --> handler : PlanChange
    alt Workspace or sprint not found (or sprint in another workspace)
      handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : SprintForm emits notFound and its dialog closes with Outdated; the opening page rereads.\nPlanning page: Sprint not found with Back to sprints, or Project not found with Back to projects\nwhen its workspace read finds no workspace
    else Workspace in Kanban mode (L2-027.3)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 sprints paused; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (sprints paused)
      client --> page : paused: keep the fields and pending sets; the plan shows read-only with the notice in the\nalert region, which takes focus; no retry; SprintForm emits modeChanged and its dialog closes with\nModeChanged: SprintsPage calls ProjectLayoutPage.modeChanged(), SprintPlanningPage increments its\ncounter so the view rereads its header
    else Sprint no longer Planned (a Closed sprint's history is never altered, L2-026.3)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 sprint started or closed; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not planned)
      client --> page : not-planned: an alert replaces the lists and takes focus; only planned sprints change here;\nlink to its board or history; no retry. SprintForm: paused presentation naming the sprint's state;\nit emits outdated, so its dialog closes with Outdated and the opening page rereads
    else Stale sprint version (L2-041.1)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 changed since opened; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (stale version)
      client --> page : Keep attempted fields and pending sets; read the latest plan once; no resubmission
      page --> actor : SprintForm shows the comparison; SprintPlanView rereads header and both lists,\ndrops marks that no longer apply and names them with neutral copy (stale state)
    else Story to add is Done or from another workspace (L2-022.2); story to remove is not a member
      handler --> ctrl : 400 identifying each story; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails per story
      client --> page : Keep pending sets; mark each named story to add with its reason (Now Done) in the\nallocated-conflict presentation; drop each named story to remove from the To remove set and name it\nneutrally ("HCK-126 is no longer in Sprint 9, so it isn't removed"), so Save plan can send the rest
    else Story to add is in another planned or active sprint (L2-022.3)
      handler --> ctrl : 409 naming each story and its sprint; nothing changed
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (already allocated)
      client --> page : Keep pending sets; mark the story (allocated-conflict state); save again after undoing it
    else Plan accepted
      handler -> entity : L2-022 editPlan(fields); applyPlanDelta(add, remove)
      note right of entity
        Only addStoryIds are new allocations.
        Existing members, Done ones included,
        stay untouched unless in removeStoryIds.
      end note
      entity --> handler : Fields; OpenSprintMembership children added and removed
      handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 AddAuditEvent; SaveChangesAsync: fields, tracked membership children,\nsuccess audit, expected version checked, one transaction
      alt Unique open-membership violation (concurrent allocation, L2-041.2)
        db --> handler : Roll back fields, membership and audit
        handler --> ctrl : 409 naming the story; nothing changed
        ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (already allocated)
        client --> page : Keep pending sets; mark the story
      else Commit fails
        db --> handler : Roll back business state and success audit
        handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
        ctrl --> client : Failure; no successful-save claim
        client --> page : Keep fields and pending sets; failed state shows the reference ID;\nSave plan sends them again only when chosen
      else Commit succeeds
        db --> handler : New sprint version
        handler --> ctrl : Saved plan header
        ctrl --> client : 200 with plan header and version
        client --> page : SprintPlanView: clear pending sets; reread header, candidate page and member page;\nemit planSaved. SprintForm: emit saved; its dialog closes with Saved(SprintSaveResult)
        page --> actor : SprintPlanView: the page shows the "Sprint planned" toast ("Sprint 9 has 3 stories.").\nSprintForm: the opening page increments its counter and shows the "Changes saved" toast
      end
    end
  end
end
note over ctrl, db
An unexpected 403 (access changed after sign-in) saves nothing; the fields and pending sets stay.
SprintPlanView emits forbidden and SprintPlanningPage shows the "Your access changed" toast through
TOAST_SERVICE, without Retry; SprintForm emits forbidden, which its dialog relays while it stays
open, and the opening page shows the same toast.
A workspace lock wait beyond the timeout returns 503 with Retry-After and no change;
the same failed state keeps fields and pending sets, shows the reference ID,
and sends them again only when Save plan is chosen.
A save that gets no response is uncertain: the fields and pending sets stay, the alert says
"We couldn't confirm whether Sprint 9's plan was saved." (no reference ID), and the page rereads
the header and both lists once, dropping marks that no longer apply under the neutral heading
"The latest plan is shown below", before Save plan is offered again; a header no longer Planned
replaces the lists with only its current state ("Sprint 9 is active now.", unconfirmed-active),
never "Nothing was changed". SprintForm emits unconfirmed,
which its dialog relays so the opening page rereads at once, and reloads the sprint: a newer
version shows the comparison under "The latest saved version is shown beside your entries".
SaveChangesAsync raises ConcurrencyConflictException on a stale version, mapped to the same 409.
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
